{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQGsbku9i7h7Jzytomk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged()`. It marks the receiver's current value as seen without taking the read lock, so afterwards `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next send. The new test passes and fails without the change.\n\n- **`tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`**: the new method sits next to `mark_changed` and has its own doc comment. It sets the receiver's version to the channel's current version, the same way `borrow_and_update` does but without borrowing the value. The version it reads has the \"closed\" flag stripped, so it works the same on a closed channel.\n- **`tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`**: the new `rx_mark_unchanged` test covers two cases: undoing a `mark_changed`, and ignoring a real `send`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- Before the method existed, the test failed to compile with `no method named mark_unchanged`.\n- `cargo test --features full --test sync_watch`: 10 passed.\n- The watch doctests: 18 passed.\n- `cargo fmt --check` is clean on both files.\n- `cargo clippy` shows only `cfg(loom)` warnings in `watch.rs` that were there before this change.\n\nI didn't run the full tokio test suite, and nothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":38380,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c649d243-fc45-4bdb-9d33-7f6699b45f1d","uuid":"d4077b75-58de-44d5-ab6b-d08687ac7c32","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:20:31.379Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQGsNNbD23tQUnz3dgX"}
